/**
 * \brief Gather items from a b2nd array of any dimensionality by flat logical coordinates.
 *
 * Fully supports arrays of any number of dimensions (1-D, 2-D, ... N-D).
 * Regardless of the array's dimensionality, every element is addressed by a
 * single flat, C-order logical index in the range {@code }[0, array->nitems){@code }
 * -- the same linearisation used by {@code }b2nd_from_cbuffer{@code } / {@code }b2nd_to_cbuffer{@code }.
 * For example, element {@code }(i, j){@code } of a 2-D array with shape {@code }(R, C){@code } has
 * flat index {@code }i * C + j{@code }; element {@code }(i, j, k){@code } of a 3-D array with shape
 * {@code }(A, B, C){@code } has flat index {@code }i * B * C + j * C + k{@code }; and so on for
 * higher dimensions.
 *
 * The function translates each flat logical coordinate to the padded storage
 * coordinate used internally by b2nd (chunk → block → item within block) and
 * then gathers the requested items into {@code }buffer{@code } in the same order as
 * {@code }coords{@code }.  Repeated and unsorted coordinates are allowed.
 *
 * This is a low-level sparse gather primitive.  It is most useful for fancy
 * indexing and as a building block for higher-level {@code }take{@code } operations.
 *
 * @param array The source b2nd array (any ndim).
 * @param ncoords Number of coordinates to gather.  May be zero.
 * @param coords Flat C-order logical coordinates in {@code }[0, array->nitems){@code }.
 *               Must not be NULL when {@code }ncoords > 0{@code }.
 * @param buffer Destination buffer.  Must have room for at least
 *               {@code }ncoords * array->sc->typesize{@code } bytes and must not be NULL
 *               when {@code }ncoords > 0{@code }.
 * @param buffersize Destination buffer size in bytes.
 *
 * @return A non-negative value on success, a negative error code otherwise.
 */
public static native int b2nd_get_sparse_cbuffer(@Const b2nd_array_t array, @Cast("int64_t") long ncoords,
                                         @Cast("const int64_t*") LongPointer coords, Pointer buffer, @Cast("int64_t") long buffersize);
public static native int b2nd_get_sparse_cbuffer(@Const b2nd_array_t array, @Cast("int64_t") long ncoords,
                                         @Cast("const int64_t*") LongBuffer coords, Pointer buffer, @Cast("int64_t") long buffersize);
public static native int b2nd_get_sparse_cbuffer(@Const b2nd_array_t array, @Cast("int64_t") long ncoords,
                                         @Cast("const int64_t*") long[] coords, Pointer buffer, @Cast("int64_t") long buffersize);


